'' RUN: member operators given operands they DO take -- an 'operator []' set over a long and
'' a string (a literal, a 'zstring * 8', a short), 'let' over a double given a long and a
'' double, '+=' over a long given a short, and a global 'operator *'. The neighbours of
'' operator-arg-nofit.test, which refuses the operands no overload takes (OperatorTakesArg_, proccheck.tiko).
'' Output identical to fbc 1.10.1's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/operator-arg-fits.bas -o tests/codegen/opargfits.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/opargfits.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/opargfits.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  6              4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  18
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  11
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  6
